  "issuedISO": "2026-11-20T08:52:00-10:00",
  "discussion": "Small surf will prevail along north- and west-facing shores for the next few days followed by much larger swells next week. A tiny north swell will be overlapped by a small north-northwest that will peak on Sunday and decline on Monday. A large northwest swell will build on Tuesday and will push surf along north- and west-facing shores well above the High Surf Advisory threshold into Wednesday. An extra large northwest swell is possible on Thanksgiving Day, though a front likely moving down the island chain at the same time could bring fresh northerly winds. Strong trade winds will maintain rough surf just below the High Surf Advisory level along east facing shores through Saturday. As trades decline, east shore surf will fall below seasonal average Sunday and will be very small through Wednesday. A small, long-period swell will bring a bump to south shore surf through Saturday, with mainly background level surf expected late Sunday through early next week.",
